est blocking move as it neutralizes the threat while occupying a key central point that limits White\'s potential connections better than blocking at K7 would.\n\nEvaluation: White has a lethal Open 3 threat on the diagonal J8-I9-H10. Black must block immediately to prevent a loss. G11 is the optimal block.\nReason: The move blocks White\'s diagonal Open 3 (J8-I9-H10) at the bottom-left end. If ignored, White would play here or at K7 to form an Open 4 and win. G11 is chosen over K7 because it prevents White from establishing a strong cluster of stones in the center (near H10/I10) and keeps Black\'s stones more connected.\nAnswer: {"col": "G", "row": 11}'}
